et and early stopping. No separate meta-learner neural network is needed. Interface: ensure the stacking XGBoost model is stored as `stacking_model`, and the feature concatenation is done smoothly.", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Remove the separate meta-learner training loop (MetaNet training, optimizer, criterion, scheduler, early stopping). Instead, train the stacking XGBoost model in a single call with early stopping (using eval_set from validation data). WHY: The two-stage pipeline is wasteful and prone to overfitting. Historical experiment #2 successfully merged pipeline steps and fixed data flow; here we simplify by collapsing meta-training into a single XGBoost training step. HOW: Delete the meta-learner training epoch loop, all MetaNet-related code. After obtaining base model predictions and DistilBERT embeddings, concatenate them into X_train_meta (training) and X_val_meta (validation). Train xgb_model_stacked = xgb.XGBClassifier(objective='multi:softprob', ...) with early_stopping_rounds, fitting on (X_train_meta, y_train) and eval_set=[(X_val_meta, y_val)]. Generate final validation and test predictions from the trained stacked model. Ensure the submission file is generated from these probabilities."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
